  "verbalization": "Rhizobialide appears to have a direct relationship with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Rhizobialide acts as a target of Isopentenyl-diphosphate Delta-isomerase, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Npc137816 and (-)-Valeranone. These intermediates are all implicated in the regulation of the kinase CDC2L1, indicating a potential pathway where Rhizobialide may influence the activity of this kinase through these metabolic intermediates. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Rhizobialide could modulate the function of CDC2L1, possibly through metabolic or signaling pathways that are regulated by these intermediates. The evidence supports a role for Rhizobialide in the regulation of CDC2L1, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
